#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2265 expect=executionError domain=DD
#expect-execution-error "group= over 'DS' has no usable key"
#note "PLAN-join-key-one-side-absent-drop QK16 (b) / QK18 (owner 2026-10-11): DS without USUBJID - the domain= call's only group= member is on the evaluated side only, so no key member is left on both sides and the rule ERRORs (never an aggregate over the whole of DS). Derived from FDA-SE2265-invalid-DD.cdt with DS.USUBJID removed. A gate declaring DS.USUBJID would turn this into a SKIP."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset DD label="Death Diagnosis"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DDSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DDTESTCD type=Char label="Death Diagnosis Short Name"
col DDORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
col DDDTC    type=Char label="Date/Time of Collection"
---
S1 | DD | 001 | 1 | DTHCAUS | HEPATIC NECROSIS | 2020-01-10
S1 | DD | 001 | 2 | DTHCAUS | HEPATIC NECROSIS | 2020-01-20
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 1 | MOVED TO RECOVERY | RECOVERY     | 2020-01-10
S1 | DS | 2 | FOUND DEAD        | DEAD         | 2020-01-20

